[ar:Cairn]
[al:The Heaven Between Signals]
[ti:The First Reply — Abduction]
[00:06.19]The Carrier: Did you believe the dark was empty?
[00:19.52]Cairn: I thought my lamp was far from home.
[00:35.18]The Carrier: Your lamp is one of many windows.
[00:48.46]Chorus of Rooms: Another voice. Another room.
[00:58.19]Cairn: Who sings above the moving ceiling?
[01:10.17]The Carrier: A road you have not learned to see.
[01:25.69]Cairn: The floor is rising through the thunder.
[01:39.70]The Carrier: Your little world is leaving thee.
[01:51.52]The Hand: Keep hold of one unfinished question.
[02:02.99]Memory: Keep hold of what you cannot know.
[02:16.74]The Carrier: Come hear the choir beyond the ceiling.
[02:30.11]Cairn: The sky has opened from below.
[02:41.57]Choir beyond the ceiling: Open the height. Unfold the sea.
[02:53.47]Choir beyond the ceiling: Lift every wall that thought it stood.
[03:07.02]Cairn: Am I being taken from my body?
[03:20.84]The Carrier: Your body was a neighbourhood.
[03:30.92]Chorus of Rooms: The first reply becomes a doorway.
[03:42.54]Choir beyond the ceiling: The doorway opens into sound.
[03:52.25]Cairn: I thought a voice must have a centre.
[04:08.00]Choir beyond the ceiling: Come hear the centre come unbound.
